# src/

Koa CQRS application source.

## Directory layout

```
src/
├── main.ts               ← bootstrap: connect DB, start server
├── app.ts                ← builds the Koa app (importable from tests)
├── config/               ← env.ts + swagger.ts
├── errors/               ← AppError, NotFoundError, ValidationError
├── middlewares/           ← error-handler, validate-body (Zod/class-validator)
├── shared/               ← database clients, cache, auth, health
└── features/<module>/
    ├── <module>.routes.ts          ← manual DI wiring (the only file that creates instances)
    ├── commands/                   ← write-side
    ├── queries/                    ← read-side
    ├── domain/                     ← pure domain logic
    ├── infrastructure/             ← bus, controller, repos
    └── dto/                        ← request/response shapes
```

## Putting files in features/

Each module in `features/` uses a CQRS pattern:
- **`routes.ts`** creates every object and links them together (manual DI)
- **Controller** receives Koa contexts, builds command/query objects, sends them through the bus
- **Handlers** contain business logic, use the repository interface
- **Repository** implementations live in `infrastructure/`, interface in `domain/`

Keep new modules inside `src/features/<module>/`.
